        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/discuss.python.org/stroxler/{size}/9681_2.png",
        "created_at": "2022-11-07T16:24:02.558Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Hi All,</p>\n<p>We’d like to put <a href=\"https://peps.python.org/pep-0698/\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\">PEP 698</a> forward for discussion.</p>\n<p>The proposal is for a new decorator <code>@typing.override</code> that marks a method as overriding a method in some superclass. Having this decorator - inspired by similar constructs in Java, C++, Typescript, Kotlin, Scala, Swift, and C# - will enable static type checkers to detect potential bugs where a base class method is renamed but child classes were not modified.</p>\n<p>Previous discussion has been on typing-sig, in particular <a href=\"https://mail.python.org/archives/list/typing-sig@python.org/thread/V23I4D6DEOFW4BBPWBMYTHZUOMKR7KQE/#UWMIPSJTJ5VFVBBRDEYWB65KRUVSCG64\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\">here is the original discussion</a>.</p>",
